# Planning document format

When creating or updating a plan for this project:

1. Start with a plain-language French section for the project owner. Explain the
   goal, the proposed direction, what changes, what stays, tradeoffs and decisions
   needed. Make it easy to evaluate the proposal quickly.
2. Include a readable visual diagram of the proposed architecture or before/after
   changes. Prefer a compact Mermaid diagram embedded in the plan.
3. Follow with an English technical section covering implementation, dependencies,
   data migration, validation, rollout and recovery as relevant to the task.
4. Use emojis sparingly, only when they convey useful meaning, such as a section's
   purpose or status. Do not add decorative emojis by default.

For example, a database integration plan first explains in French how data moves
between devices and the backend, then details schema, access control and sync in
English. This format applies to plans, not to application copy or every answer.
